WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.500
Step 1: As an OpStack owner, open Console → Billing. Start in Sandbox, enter the Stripe test secret key and save. Keep Live and Sandbox credentials separate; blank secret fields preserve the saved values.

2
00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:22.375
Step 2: Set APP_ORIGIN to the public HTTPS app address. Create the displayed webhook endpoint in Stripe with API version 2024-06-20, for checkout.session.completed, customer.subscription.*, invoice.* and charge.refunded. Save its matching signing secret.

3
00:00:22.375 --> 00:00:32.333
Step 3: Choose Test connection &amp; sync. Check Connected and the last report sync. Imports read every page before replacing the previous results; failures retain the last completed report.

4
00:00:32.333 --> 00:00:47.583
Step 4: Create a customer and two recurring AUD monthly per-unit prices in Stripe. Add the location, customer ID, location price and user price, then save. Use the same customer for locations paid by the same business; shared activated staff count once per customer and network.

5
00:00:47.583 --> 00:01:05.333
Step 5: Review billing and check the rates, user count and tax treatment. For a new subscription, create the hosted checkout link and let the customer finish it. Sync, then review and apply quantities. For automatic updates, select the plan checkbox, save and review/apply, then enable automatic sync. Changes prorate on the next invoice.

6
00:01:05.333 --> 00:01:19.667
Step 6: Open Monthly report → Collections for linked paid invoices, open amounts, refunds and uncollectible invoices. Choose Sandbox explicitly for test results. Manage taxes, receipts, refunds and cancellations in Stripe. Stop old GoCardless subscriptions there before starting Stripe to avoid double billing.
